From a461e65e26e10287ca3d817786290be26bcf0127 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <a@b>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:03:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] cpufreq: qcom-hw: honour the ACD bring-up gate steps on
 SoCs without ACD

qcom_cpufreq_hw_acd_init() returned 0 before its step 8-10 checks when
the SoC has no ACD region (SDM630/660). The caller then wrote PERF_STATE
and the OSM enable bit and only stopped at the step 11 check, so
osm_setup_stop=8..10 enabled the OSM on SDM660, contrary to the gate's
documentation. Stop at step 10 in the no-ACD path as well.
---
 drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
index 4a4856668..6ba798a82 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c
@@ -816,9 +816,17 @@ static int qcom_cpufreq_hw_acd_init(struct device *cpu_dev,
 
 	snprintf(acd_resname, sizeof(acd_resname), "osm-acd%d", index);
 
-	/* ACD is optional (SDM630/660 have none): no region, nothing to do */
+	/*
+	 * ACD is optional (SDM630/660 have none): no region, nothing to do.
+	 * Still honour the ACD steps of the bring-up gate. Returning 0 here
+	 * made osm_setup_stop=8..10 fall through to the OSM enable write on
+	 * SoCs without ACD, so "any N below 11 leaves the OSM disabled" was
+	 * false on SDM660.
+	 */
 	if (!platform_get_resource_byname(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, acd_resname)) {
 		dev_vdbg(cpu_dev, "Skipping ACD initialization.\n");
+		if (qcom_cpufreq_osm_stop_after(cpu_dev, index, 10, "acd-none"))
+			return -ECANCELED;
 		return 0;
 	}
 
